# PlatformIO / ESP-IDF build output. Regenerated on every build; never a
# source of truth.
.pio/

# ESP-IDF's per-environment generated sdkconfig (merged from
# sdkconfig.defaults* + board defaults). Only the sdkconfig.defaults*
# inputs are tracked; the generated sdkconfig.<env> files are build output.
sdkconfig.teleop
sdkconfig.production
# teleop-bringup task 7.1: [env:bench] layers the same sdkconfig.defaults.teleop
# (research.md "Decision: E-3 の開ループ確認を teleop 系の第3プロファイルとして
# 分離する" -- kept in the teleop family rather than a 4th sdkconfig layer), so
# it gets its own generated sdkconfig.bench, same build-output category as the
# two above.
sdkconfig.bench

# ESP-IDF Component Manager's resolved-dependency lock file. Regenerated at
# configure time (first appeared once [env:teleop] started resolving
# idf_component.yml manifests -- Bluepad32 ships one, per teleop-bringup
# task 5.1). Same category as sdkconfig.<env> above: a build output, not a
# source of truth.
dependencies.lock

# teleop-bringup task 5.1 (requirements.md 7.1): Bluepad32 + BTstack,
# fetched on demand by scripts/fetch_bluepad32.py ([env:teleop] extra_scripts
# only). ⚠️ Deliberately never vendored: BTstack's license permits personal
# use only, not commercial use or monetary gain (README.md "ライセンスと
# 再配布上の制約"). Committing its source would redistribute it with this
# repository regardless of which profile a given clone ever builds.
# fetch_bluepad32.py pins an immutable upstream tag and records the resolved
# commit hashes in .deps/bluepad32/.fetch_bluepad32.json for reproducibility.
.deps/
